==Russian==
[[Category:Russian nouns]]
===Etymology===
From Common Slavonic {{term|брѣгъ|sc=Cyrs}} from {{proto|Indo-European|bʰergʰ|height|lang=cu}}. Cognate with {{proto|Germanic|bergoz}}, (English {{term|barrow}}, German {{term|Berg}}), Old Irish {{term|brigh||mountain}}, Armenian {{term|բարձր|sc=Arme||high|tr=bardzr}}.

===Noun===
'''берег''' (béreg) {{m}}
:N.B.— ''The irregular plural [[берега]] is actually an old dual form, since rivers have two of them.''

# [[bank]], [[shore]], [[coast]], [[beach]]
# [[land]]

